WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.830
The River Tees rises in the North Pennines
and flows south-east to the North Sea

2
00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:06.330
at Teesside.

3
00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:10.030
High in the dales, it pours
over three waterfalls:

4
00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:13.570
Cauldron Snout, High Force and Low Force.

5
00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:18.030
Lower down, near Yarm, it
crosses a broad, low plain.

6
00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:22.110
There it winds slowly
between steep, wooded banks.

7
00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:23.330
One river.

8
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:27.080
So why a cliff in one place,
and lazy loops in another?

9
00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:30.250
In this mission, you'll find
out how a waterfall forms,

10
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.790
and why it creeps upstream.

11
00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:35.530
Then you'll follow the
river down to its meanders,

12
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.350
floodplain and estuary mudflats.

13
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:43.430
Your mission: explain why the Tees has
waterfalls in the uplands but loops across

14
00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:44.830
its lowland plain.
